<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas Carleton</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1735–<a href="/years/1817">1817</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thomas Carleton (c. 1735–1817) was an Irish-born British army officer who became the first governor of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a> when it was separated from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a> in 1784 to receive Loyalist refugees. He chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fredericton">Fredericton</a> as the capital and set up the colony's institutions. He left for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1803 but formally held the post until his death.</p></div>
